{"at":"2026-10-04T12:54:14.662Z","toolCall":{"args":{"Arguments":{"conclusion":"The `--network none` flag completely isolates the container's networking stack, creating only an IPv4 loopback device (no IPv6 loopback address is configured).","content":"If you want to completely isolate the networking stack of a container, you can use the --network none flag when starting the container. Within the container, only the loopback device is created. No IPv6 loopback address is configured for containers using the none driver.","scope":"Supported container network-none behavior","source":"https://docs.docker.com/engine/network/drivers/none/"},"ServerName":"project_architect","ToolName":"evidence_record","toolAction":"Recording evidence","toolSummary":"Record evidence"},"name":"call_mcp_tool"},"decision":"allow","stepIdx":30,"imagePath":null}
